hello everyone i would like to welcome  you all for the webinar today on a very  exciting topic that is spaceomics  that is dedicated to the study of omix  data to study molecular mechanisms  affected by the space travel and  critical for astronaut health as well  so as we have a lot of new participants  joining us today i would like to first  of all introduce what space omix is all  about and then we listen to the mentors  discussing about the various research  project opportunities in the domain  itself  so astrobiology is a science which  addresses the origin of life on earth  and potential for life elsewhere in the  universe as well  space flight is one of the most extreme  conditions that has been encountered by  humans  and advances in omix methodology such as  genomics transcriptomics proteomics and  metabolomics have revealed that unique  differences exist between individuals  these differences can be amplified in  extreme conditions such as space flight  a better understanding of individual  differences may allow us to develop  personalized counter measure packages  that optimize the safety and performance  of each astronaut  radiation microgravity altered  atmospheric gas composition isolation  and diet changes are just some of the  known stressors affecting humans in the  space environment  with extended mission durations and  distances outside of the earth's orbit  these factors are expected to increase  there are several adverse human health  effects associated with space flight  including bone demineralization skeletal  muscle atrophy cardiovascular  deconditioning vestibular control immune  system suppression and neuro ocular  ailments as well so it is critical to  understand how space flight factors  affect human health in order to develop  space a safe and effective counter  measures  the nasa twin study catalyzed the need  for more comprehensive consortium-based  approaches to study the long-term  effects of space flight on humans here a  nine research group studied a single  data type in detail which another group  performed multi-org synthesis uh to  determine the whole body changes the  study identified alterations in numerous  data types including telomere length  gene regulation gut microbiome  composition body weight carotid artery  dimensions and serum metabolite profiles  as well  so before we start with the talk i would  like to introduce us we are a u.s based  bioinformatics company who is working  with multiple academic and commercial  collaborators to develop easy to use  analytical tools and our mission here is  to make bioinformatics more accessible  our mixed logic research-based training  programs are a result of close  collaboration between pine biotech and  numerous academic institutions that have  participated in content evaluation  curriculum review and project design  omixlogic is an international program  that is running in five different  regions with over 10 000 users around  the world and due to this fast growth  our team is working with local and  regional coordinators that are helping  refine local program logistics and  leverage our online training resources  as well adapting them to the needs of  students and researchers around the  world  my name is sunali khari and i'm the  omixlogic community manager i'm  responsible for daily interaction with  thousands of users that are a part of  our bioinformatics community managed by  biotech  our training is designed to allow  participants to apply methods to curated  and new data sets  and develop independent projects that  showcase what has been learned in the  context of a personal portfolio of  projects  as a result anyone starting on this  journey in bioinformatics can start  developing a project of their own  so together with our existing modules  for which you will gain access to the  omixlogic portal where you can try and  explore these modules exercises and  pipeline building coding and various  methods of analysis using projects or  resources from peer-reviewed  publications  now i would like to pass on the stage to  subrajeed bharwan delara dicken to talk  about their astrobiology projects and  experience as well  suprajet barua is an ms in molecular  biology and biotechnology at the  international scam laboratory itamo  university saint petersburg russia he is  a graduate of red school 2021 latex  french exobiology society he is an  astrobiology educator at art of inquiry  where he works closely with julia  brodsky former nasa iess astronaut  trainer he is also a volunteer at mars  on earth project where he works on  margin projects he is a russian  government open door scholar and a  president scholarship awardee as well he  was also one of the top 10 students  globally selected for sgac space health  risk symposium london 2021  we are pleased to have you with us  subrajeet over to you  thank you so much  for that wonderful  presentation  and hello to everyone who has joined
 

